            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Economic Policies</strong><br>\nDuring his presidency, Nixon faced economic challenges, including inflation and a recession. He controversially implemented wage and price controls to curb inflation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Watergate Scandal</strong><br>\nThe Watergate scandal was a major event in Nixon's presidency, leading to his resignation in 1974 to avoid impeachment over the break-in at the Democratic National Committee and subsequent cover-up.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years</strong><br>\nAfter resigning from the presidency, Nixon spent his later years engaged in writing and commentary on public affairs, rehabilitating his public image until his death on April 22, 1994.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
